## 0. What this text is, in plain words
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This license covers the files in this repository (the "Materials"). It says what you may do with those files.

It is written by the author of the Materials to be read by engineers. Five things are stated up front so that nobody has
to infer them:

1. Tau Language is not the author's. Tau Language and the logics it implements are the work of Ohad Asor; Tau Language,
   its engine, its syntax and semantics are developed and owned by IDNI AG. Nothing here grants any right to Tau
   Language (section 2).
2. A license governs files. This license governs the use of the Materials by those who take them under it. It is not a
   patent, it is not a patent license, and it does not claim to be either (section 9).
3. This license describes a method. It does not assert that any deployed system has been shown to be fair, and it does
   not assert that the Materials contain a complete implementation of the method (section 4).
4. This license covers the Materials in this repository. A paper by the author that describes the method is a separate
   work under its own license (Creative Commons BY-NC-ND 4.0); that license concerns the text of the paper, and this one
   concerns the files here. The paper describes the executions X1 and X2 of section 3.2; the execution X3 is described
   in this license and in the earlier texts of the author named there.
5. Commercial Use of the Tutorial Materials, of the Method Materials and — for those who take the Materials — of the
   Method requires a written license from the author, in every context (sections 7 and 8). Earlier versions of this
   license granted Commercial Use within a named ecosystem; this version does not. The author may change this license
   for future releases at any time; changes are not retroactive (section 10).

