## 1. Definitions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Materials" means every file in this repository at the release that carries this license text, including specification
files (`.tau`), runner scripts, expected-result contracts, input samples, and documentation, with the one exception
named at the end of this section.

"Method Materials" means those Materials that express the Method or a part of it: `casino.tau`,
`temporal_state_machine.tau`, and every file added to this repository that states in its header that it belongs to the
Method Materials.

"Tutorial Materials" means the Tau-Nomic Tutorial Series and the other teaching files: every file whose name begins with
`nomic_`, and `consensus_decomposed.tau`, `nomic_run_all.sh`, `adt_tutorial_basic.tau`, `adt_tutorial_advanced.tau`,
`adt_tables_basic.tau`, `adt_tables_advanced.tau`, `adt_tables_beyond_sql.tau`, `testing_done_right.tau`,
`values_without_places.tau`, `adaptive_memory_management.tau`, together with their expected-result contracts — and every
file in this repository that is neither listed as Classic Material nor marked as Method Material (the default).

"Classic Materials" means exactly these files: `4bit_binary_adder.tau`, `4bit_binary_adder_io.tau`,
`4bit_binary_adder_sbf.tau`, `4bit_binary_substractor.tau`, `4bit_binary_multiplier.tau`, `logic_gates.tau`,
`binary_encoding.tau`, `bitvector_tutorial.tau`, `barber_demo_1.tau`, `barber_demo_2.tau`, `temporal_stability.tau`,
`temporal_meta_prediction.tau`, `delayed_signal.tau`, `feedback_loop.tau`, and the files under `io/`.

"The Method" has the meaning given in section 3.

"Commercial Use" means any use that is primarily intended for, or directed toward, commercial advantage or monetary
compensation. It includes operating a service for which users or third parties pay in any form (stakes, fees,
subscriptions, advertising, tokens), including a free tier of such a service; integrating the Materials into a product
that is sold or licensed; and providing the Materials or works derived from them to others for payment. Research,
evaluation and verification whose purpose is to understand, test or check the Materials or the Method are not Commercial
Use, also when carried out inside a company. Operational use inside a business — running the Materials or the Method to
settle rounds, make, prepare or support decisions, offers or actions of that business or of its customers — is
Commercial Use, whether or not a product is sold.

"Training" means using the Materials, in whole or in part, as input for training, fine-tuning or distilling a
machine-learning model, or for text and data mining. Running a model against the Materials for research is not Training.

A person "takes the Materials" when they obtain a copy of any part of them from any source and use, run, copy, modify or
distribute it; reading alone is not taking. A person acting for a company or for its contractors takes the Materials for
that company and for every affiliate of it that makes use of the result.



Not part of the Materials: the archive `tdr-0.5-windows-TAUMORROW.zip`. It is an earlier program that is no longer
maintained; it remains under the terms it was released with, and this license says nothing further about it.

