   revoked by this one. If you obtained a release under an earlier license, that release stays under that license for
   you.

2. **Nothing here is retroactive.** This text applies to v4.0 and later, until a later release ships a different text.
   Where this text places a file in a different class than an earlier text did, that applies to the file as it appears
   in v4.0 and later; the file as it appeared in an earlier release stays under the terms of that release.

3. **Future versions may have different terms, at any time.** The author may change the license for future releases at
   any time and for any reason. Changes are not retroactive: the grants and the agreement of section 8 for a release
   stay as they are in the text under which that release was taken.

4. **Which text applies.** Each release carries its license in the `LICENSE` file at that commit. If you build on the
   Materials, pin a commit.

